 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Of course. Make sure you and he have a routine before daddy comes. Get dressed and take a walk every day. He' appreciate the consistency. Try saying where things are just after he says he needs them, like 'my room for my clothes, and the kitchen for my lunch. Try outings he' remember, like the shop where he buys your mum's favourite chocolate, or the park where he falls a lot while walking. Avoid new ones. Be patient. He won't remember everything, and some days are just going to be rough. Offer him your support instead.",
